alues":["ONE WORKFLOW — FOUR MAP SWITCHES\n\n1. Browse Movie Frames or upload a reference in the Reference Browser.\n2. Turn ON the map you want. With exactly one ON, generation_control=auto loads its tested adapter. All OFF generates from the prompt only.\n3. Multiple maps may be ON for inspection. Choose generation_control explicitly: that map guides generation; the other maps are previews only. Auto with multiple maps stops with a clear error. Simultaneous mixed-adapter guidance is NOT validated or silently approximated.\n4. The Control Panel status shows the actual selected adapter; STALE means settings changed since its last execution.\n\nPROMPTING\nWrite subject + action + environment + lighting. Match the reference camera direction unless you intentionally want weaker structural adherence. Your prompt is passed verbatim, without hidden rewriting. A map guides geometry; it does not preserve identity or guarantee a specified lens angle. For a visible face, use a reference that makes the face readable.\n\nQUALITY CHECK\nInspect the fixed map previews first. Pose constrains the person; depth guides scene structure; Canny and lineart constrain outlines. Enable optional style LoRAs only after checking a baseline. Avoid adding control adapters to the style stack; routing already loads the required adapter. Keep the seed fixed when comparing settings.\n\nSAMPLING\nsteps_override=0 uses tested mode settings: Pose 10 Euler; Depth/Canny 8 Euler; Lineart 8 Euler ancestral. CFG=1, scheduler=simple, denoise=1. Route failures stop generation rather than dropping guidance.\n\nSame map switches and browser stay in this one file.\n\nPUBLIC DEMO\nChoose your installed Krea Turbo / text encoder / VAE filenames, and load a suitable real reference. The geometric demo asset only demonstrates the UI and mask editor. No reference image or prompt from a private project is included."]}],"links":[[1,1,0,2,0,"IMAGE"],[2,2,0,3,0,"DHARANI_CONTROL_PLAN"],[3,3,0,4,0,"DHARANI_RENDER_RECIPE"],